## Conclusion
The host's fused merge raises versions of modules PiG already requires (flock) but does not add the modules the member needs that PiG's go.mod lacks (readability, html-to-markdown, gonja, gotreesitter, doublestar, tomledit, mvdan sh, ...). Under -mod=readonly the link fails. A member whose dependencies are a subset of PiG's module graph fuses (minimal Go extension and the api-only reference producer do). Not a Workbench defect: Workbench's own go.mod lists every requirement. Fix belongs in the PiG fused-member merge (run go mod tidy or add the member's requirements).
